          "# Database Structure\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe database structure defines the data models, relationships, and access patterns used throughout the PolygonExpress back-end. It provides a consistent interface for data operations while maintaining type safety and integrity.\n\n## Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    DBClient[Database Client] --> ConnectionPool[Connection Pool]\n    DBClient --> QueryBuilder[Query Builder]\n    DBClient --> Migrations[Migration System]\n    \n    QueryBuilder --> UserRepository[User Repository]\n    QueryBuilder --> OrderRepository[Order Repository]\n    QueryBuilder --> ProductRepository[Product Repository]\n    \n    subgraph \"Database Core\"\n        DBClient\n        ConnectionPool\n        QueryBuilder\n        Migrations\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Repositories\"\n        UserRepository\n        OrderRepository\n        ProductRepository\n    end\n```\n\n## Database Models\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, Integer, String, Float, ForeignKey, DateTime\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import relationship\nfrom app.db.base import Base\n\nclass User(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"users\"\n    \n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)\n    username = Column(String, unique=True, index=True)\n    email = Column(String, unique=True, index=True)\n    hashed_password = Column(String)\n    \n    orders = relationship(\"Order\", back_populates=\"user\")\n\nclass Product(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"products\"\n    \n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)\n    name = Column(String, index=True)\n    description = Column(String)\n    price = Column(Float)\n    \n    order_items = relationship(\"OrderItem\", back_populates=\"product\")\n\nclass Order(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"orders\"\n    \n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)\n    user_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"users.id\"))\n    status = Column(String)\n    created_at = Column(DateTime)\n    updated_at = Column(DateTime)\n    \n    user = relationship(\"User\", back_populates=\"orders\")\n    items = relationship(\"OrderItem\", back_populates=\"order\")\n\nclass OrderItem(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"order_items\"\n    \n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)\n    order_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"orders.id\"))\n    product_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"products.id\"))\n    quantity = Column(Integer)\n    price = Column(Float)\n    \n    order = relationship(\"Order\", back_populates=\"items\")\n    product = relationship(\"Product\", back_populates=\"order_items\")\n```\n\n## Database Access Patterns\n\n### Repository Pattern\n\nAll database access is performed through repository classes that provide type-safe CRUD operations:\n\n```python\nclass BaseRepository:\n    def __init__(self, db_session):\n        self.db_session = db_session\n    \n    def get_all(self):\n        raise NotImplementedError()\n    \n    def get_by_id(self, id):\n        raise NotImplementedError()\n    \n    def create(self, obj_in):\n        raise NotImplementedError()\n    \n    def update(self, id, obj_in):\n        raise NotImplementedError()\n    \n    def delete(self, id):\n        raise NotImplementedError()\n\nclass UserRepository(BaseRepository):\n    def get_all(self):\n        return self.db_session.query(User).all()\n    \n    def get_by_id(self, id):\n        return self.db_session.query(User).filter(User.id == id).first()\n    \n    # Additional methods...\n```\n\n## Related Components\n\n- [Database Configuration](./configuration.md) - Database connection settings\n- [Migration System](./migrations.md) - Schema migration process\n- [Data Validation](../models/validation.md) - Pydantic models for data validation")

